(*"aic_curve_swept_solid.curve_swept_solid_shape_representation"
A *curve_swept_solid_shape_representation* is a type of <<express:product_property_representation_schema.shape_representation,shape_representation>> in which the shape of a product is represented by specialisations of <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid,swept_area_solid>> or <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid,swept_disk_solid>> entities.

Each <<express:geometric_model_schema.solid_model,solid_model>> in the <<express:representation_schema.representation,representation>> is required to be a <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid,swept_area_solid>> or a <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid,swept_disk_solid>>.

Particular types of <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid,swept_area_solid>> that may be included are <<express:geometric_model_schema.extruded_area_solid,extruded_area_solid>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.revolved_area_solid,revolved_area_solid>>, and <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid,surface_curve_swept_area_solid>>, including the <<express:aic_curve_swept_solid.ruled_surface_swept_area_solid,ruled_surface_swept_area_solid>>.
*)

(*"aic_curve_swept_solid.curve_swept_solid_shape_representation.wr:WR1"
The <<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> in a *curve_swept_solid_shape_representation* shall be <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid,swept_area_solid>>, <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid,swept_disk_solid>>, <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>, or <<express:geometry_schema.axis2_placement_3d,axis2_placement_3d>>.
*)

(*"aic_curve_swept_solid.curve_swept_solid_shape_representation.wr:WR2"
At least one of the <<express:representation_schema.representation.items,items>> shall be either a <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid,swept_area_solid>>, a <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_disk_solid,swept_disk_solid>> or a <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>.
*)

(*"aic_curve_swept_solid.curve_swept_solid_shape_representation.wr:WR3"
For any <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item,mapped_item>>, the <<express:representation_schema.representation_map.mapped_representation,mapped_representation>> of its <<express:representation_schema.mapped_item.mapping_source,mapping_source>> shall be a *curve_swept_solid_shape_representation*.
*)

(*"aic_curve_swept_solid.curve_swept_solid_shape_representation.wr:WR4"
If there is a <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid,surface_curve_swept_area_solid>> in a *curve_swept_solid_shape_representation* the <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.directrix,directrix>> shall be either a <<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> or a <<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>>.
*)

(*"aic_curve_swept_solid.ruled_surface_swept_area_solid"
A *ruled_surface_swept_area_solid* is a type of <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid,surface_curve_swept_area_solid>> in which the surface used to control the orientation of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>> as it is swept along the <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.directrix,directrix>> is a ruled surface. The ruled surface is required to be defined as a <<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>> of degree 1 in the first parameter direction.

[NOTE]
--
At all times during the sweeping operation the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>> is maintained in the plane normal to the <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.directrix,directrix>> and is oriented by keeping the x axis of the plane (z = 0) of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>> in the direction of the normal to the ruled surface at the current point on the <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.directrix,directrix>>. This implies that the negative y axis of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.swept_area_solid.swept_area,swept_area>> plane lies in the direction of the projection of the ruling direction onto the plane normal to the <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.directrix,directrix>>.
--
*)

(*"aic_curve_swept_solid.ruled_surface_swept_area_solid.wr:WR1"
The <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.reference_surface,reference_surface>> of a *ruled_surface_swept_area_solid* shall be a <<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface,b_spline_surface>> surface of <<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface.u_degree,u_degree>> 1.

[NOTE]
--
This ensures that the reference surface has the form of a ruled surface bounded by two <<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>>. These curves have degree <<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface.v_degree,v_degree>> and are defined by the two sub-lists of the <<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_surface.control_points_list,control_points_list>> of the <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.reference_surface,reference_surface>>.
--
*)

(*"aic_curve_swept_solid.ruled_surface_swept_area_solid.wr:WR2"
The <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.directrix,directrix>> shall be either a <<express:geometry_schema.pcurve,pcurve>> or a <<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>>. If the <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.directrix,directrix>> is a <<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve,surface_curve>> the <<express:geometry_schema.surface_curve.curve_3d,curve_3d>> shall be a <<express:geometry_schema.b_spline_curve,b_spline_curve>> of the same degree as the boundary curves of the ruled surface that is the <<express:geometric_model_schema.surface_curve_swept_area_solid.reference_surface,reference_surface>>.
*)
